&P351410 = ARM 14, 070 
#atf: lang akk 
@tablet 
@obverse 
1.  a-na be-li2-ia qi2-bi2-ma# 
#tr.en: Say to my lord, 
2. um-ma ia-qi2-im-{d}iszkur 
#tr.en: thus Yaqim-Addu 
3. _ARAD2_-ka-a-ma 
#tr.en: your servant: 
4. be-li2 ki-a-am isz-pu-ra-am um-ma-a-mi 
#tr.en: My lord wrote thus: 
5. s,a-bu-um _babila_{ki} sza i-na sa-ga-ra-tim{ki} 
#tr.en: 'Let the Babylonian army that is stationed 
6. wa-szi-ib i-na sa-ga-ra-tim#{ki} s,i2-di-tam 
#tr.en: at Sagaratum receive provisions in Sagaratum 
7. li-im-hu-ur u3 sza [i]-na  _bad3_{ki}-ia-ah-du-li-im 
#tr.en: and have the one that is stationed at Dur-Yahdu-Lim 
8. wa-szi-ib# i-na _bad3_{ki}-ia#-ah-du-li-im-ma 
#tr.en: receive provisions at Dur-Yahdu-Lim. 
9. s,i2#-[di]-tam# szu-um-hi-ir-ma# s,a-ba-am sze-tu 
#tr.en: Send that army and  
10. [u3 s,a]-ba#-am sza tu-sza-at,-t,e4-ru 
#tr.en: the army that you have registered.' 
11. [t,u2-ur]-dam _ud_ 5(disz) _kam_ pa-an mu-szi-im tup-pi2 be-li2-ia 
#tr.en: The tablet of my lord arrived on the 5th day before nightfall. 
12. [ik-szu]-dam# la#-ma# tup-pi2 be-li2-ia i-ka-asz-sza-dam 
#tr.en: Before the tablet of my lord arrived, 
13. [x x x tup?-pi2? ni]-id#-na-at-{d}suen 
#tr.en: ... [the tablet?] of Nidnat-Sin... 
14. [... s,a-bu-um] _babila#_{ki} 
#tr.en: ... [the army?] of Babylon 
15. [...] tup-pi2 be-li2-ia 
#tr.en: [...] my lord's tablet. 
$ rest broken 
@reverse 
$ beginning broken 
1'. [...] x-u2 i-na# pu-lu-uh-ti be-li2-ia 
#tr.en: ...because of fear of my lord 
2'. [u2-sza]-asz2#-t,i2-ir i-na tup-pi2 te-<bi>-ib-ti 
#tr.en: I had it written. In my lord's registration tablet  
3'. ha#-al-s,i-im sza a-na s,e-er be-li2-ia 
#tr.en: for the district which I sent back to him, 
4'. u2-sza-bi-lam hi-im-mu-um sza-t,e4-er 
#tr.en:  a 'himmum' is written. 
5'. i-na#-an-na szum-ma i-in be-li2-ia ma-hi-ir 
#tr.en: Now if it pleases my lord, 
6'. [be-li2] li-isz-ta-al-ma  _lu2-szu-gi_  u3 _lu2-tur-mesz_ 
#tr.en: let him consider if I should assign the old men 
7'. sza  _kaskal_ a-la-kam la i-le-u2 lu-u2 lu-bi-ir-ma 
#tr.en: and the young ones who cannot go on the campaign 
8'. a-na ma-as,-s,a-ar-ti _dur3_{ki} u2-lu-ma 
#tr.en: to guard the wall  
9'. a-szar be-li2 i-qa-ab-bu-u2 li-si-qu2!(BA)-szu-nu-ti 
#tr.en: or the place my lord my lord orders,  
10'. u3 s,a-ba-am be2-eh-ra-am lu-bi-ra-am-ma 
#tr.en: and choosing the elite army 
11'. ki-ma na-asz-pa-ar-ti be-li2-ia lu-ut,-ru-dam 
#tr.en: send them to my lord as per his instructions. 
12'. an-ni-tam la an-ni-tam be-li2 li-isz-pu-ra-am 
#tr.en: Let my lord write to me whether this should be so. 
13'. u3 as-su2-ur-ri be-li2 ki-a-am i-qa-ab-bi# 
#tr.en: Perhaps my lord will say: 
14'. um#-ma-a-mi s,a-bu-um _babila_{ki} i-zi-iz 
#tr.en: 'The Babylonian army will be upset.' 
15'. ki-ma _lu2-mesz_ tap-pi2-szu i-na e-s,e2-di-im 
#tr.en: Like their compatriots, I have 
16'. u2-ne-eh mi-im-ma s,a-bu-um szu-u2 
#tr.en: exempted them from service. 
17'. [u2]-ul i-s,i2-id i-na sza-ni-im 
#tr.en: That army has not been gathered. 
@left 
18'. u4-mi-im sza a-na sa-ga-ra-tim{ki} 
#tr.en: Following the day that they arrive 
19'. ik-szu-du-nim tup-pi2 ni-id-na-at-{d}suen# 
#tr.en: in Sagaratum and the tablet of Nidnat-Sin 
20'. ik-szu-dam-ma ip-t,u2-ru-nim#? 
#tr.en: comes to me, they will be released.

